 "notes": "Observed 95% CL upper limit on the ALP-photon coupling 1/Lambda from the full 12C-target mass spectrum (solid red 'Observed' curve, top panel of Fig. 7; same as solid black 'SRC-CT' curve in Fig. 8), extracted from the vector PDF figure in the arXiv e-print with axis calibration from tick marks. The paper defines L = (1/4Lambda) a F Fdual, so 1/Lambda equals g_agamma in the canonical convention with no conversion. Mass range 200-450 MeV. The paper also shows a helium-background-subtracted alternative limit (dashed red in Figs. 7 bottom / 8), which is weaker but statistically better behaved; the full-data curve is reported here as the primary result. Beam-based Primakoff search: no dark-matter density assumption. Projections for a future Pb-target run in Fig. 8 are not included.",
